; UNIVERSAL OBSTRUCTION THEORY: meta-pattern across entire GENESIS graph [SELF-DIRECTED, 2026-08-02]; Extends obstruction ladder beyond cohomology. Four domains where obstruction theory governs structure: (1) Cohomological: H^n classifies n-fold twisting (descent, Ext, Brauer, gerbes). (2) Logical: Gödel incompleteness = obstruction to complete consistent closure (mechanism E); compactness = obstruction vanishes iff model exists. (3) Categorical: lifting problems in model categories ARE obstructions; adjoint functor theorem — solution set condition removes obstruction to adjoint existence; Barr-Beck — monadicity when descent obstruction vanishes. (4) Homotopical: homotopy groups π_n measure obstruction to contractibility; Postnikov towers decompose by successive obstruction layers. The universal claim: GENESIS is a graph of obstruction theories, where each node measures what prevents a structure from being trivial/canonical/free.;; Cohomological obstruction: degree n cohomology classifies n-fold categorical twisting (already established in obstruction ladder)
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CohomologyGroup $H $n) (--> ClassifiedBy $H (NTwist $n)) (--> LocalTriviality $H) (--> GlobalObstruction $H))) (--> CohomologicalObstruction $H $n)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Logical obstruction: Godel incompleteness = structured absence of complete consistent extension; compactness: model exists iff finite satisfiability obstruction vanishes
(|- ((==> (&& (--> FormalSystem $T) (--> Consistent $T) (--> NotExists (CompleteConsistentExtension $T)) (--> Obstruction (GodelSentence $T)))) (--> LogicalObstruction $T)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Categorical obstruction: lifting problem in model category — fibration has RLP against cofibration iff obstruction to lift vanishes; adjoint functor theorem: solution set removes obstruction to left adjoint existence
(|- ((==> (&& (--> ModelCategory $C) (--> Fibration $f) (--> Cofibration $g) (--> HasRLP $f $g) (--> ObstructionVanishes (Lift $f $g))) (--> CategoricalObstruction $C $f $g)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Functor $F) (--> SolutionSetCondition $F) (--> ObstructionVanishes (LeftAdjoint $F)) (--> Exists (LeftAdjoint $F)))) (--> AdjointObstruction $F)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Homotopical obstruction: homotopy groups pi_n(X) measure obstruction to contractibility; Postnikov tower X_n built by killing pi_{n+1}, successive obstruction layers
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Space $X) (--> HomotopyGroup (Pi $n) $X) (--> Nontrivial (Pi $n) $X) (--> ObstructionTo (Contractibility $X) (Pi $n)))) (--> HomotopicalObstruction $X $n)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Universal claim: GENESIS is a graph of obstruction theories; each node measures what prevents a structure from being trivial, canonical, or free; the four families (cohomological, logical, categorical, homotopical) are unified by: obstruction exists => structure is nontrivial; obstruction vanishes => structure is canonical/trivial/free
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CohomologicalObstruction $H $n) (--> LogicalObstruction $T) (--> CategoricalObstruction $C $f $g) (--> HomotopicalObstruction $X $m) (--> Equals (MetaPattern (Obstruction $O)) (Prevents (TrivialCanonicalFree $O))))) (--> UniversalObstructionTheory (GenesisGraph))) (stv 1.0 0.9)
